  "versionNotes":[{"edition":".NET 11 GA checked 2026-11-14","items":["The built-in DI container in .NET 11 attempts to dispose every captured disposable service even if one disposal throws; multiple failures are aggregated in AggregateException. Keyed services remain part of the built-in container surface, and .NET 10 changed GetKeyedService(KeyedService.AnyKey) to throw because AnyKey is not a key for resolving one service."],"sourceUrls":["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/core/compatibility/extensions/11/dependency-injection-disposal-exceptions","https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/core/extensions/dependency-injection"]}],
